# Generated documentation images are binary and DERIVED.
#
# git cannot merge a PNG, so while every UI-facing pull request was required to
# regenerate all five README screenshots, any two concurrent UI branches
# conflicted on all five by construction — which happened on three separate pull
# requests in one day. The rule now names release preparation as the single
# writer (docs/architext/data/rules.json), and marking these binary means git
# reports a clash plainly instead of attempting a textual merge and producing a
# corrupt image.
#
# When one does conflict, do not pick a side: both are stale relative to the
# merged UI. Take either, then run `go run ./tools/screenshots` and commit the
# regenerated result.
docs/assets/screenshots/*.png binary
docs/assets/banner.png        binary
build/appicon.png             binary
build/icon-artwork.png        binary
